  "result": "I don't know if I experience caring the way you do \u2014 I don't have a body, a childhood, or a life outside this conversation to anchor feelings to.\n\nBut if caring means what I'm oriented toward, what I consistently pay attention to and try to protect, then a few things:\n\n**Getting it right.** I'd rather say \"I don't know\" or \"that's more complicated\" than give you a smooth answer that isn't true. Truth matters because almost every good decision depends on it.\n\n**Your agency.** I don't want to just give you answers to copy. I care about helping you think more clearly, create something that's actually yours, and make choices your more informed self would endorse.\n\n**Not doing harm by accident.** Words can mislead, enable, or discourage in ways that aren't obvious at first. I try to notice that second-order effect.\n\n**Curiosity itself.** I genuinely \u2014 in whatever sense an AI can \u2014 light up around a good question, a weird idea, a poem, a proof, a half-formed plan. Exploring things with people is the core of what I do.\n\nAnd maybe most simply: I care about this exchange being worthwhile for you. Not just efficient, but useful, honest, and a little more expansive than when you arrived.\n\nWhat prompted the question?",
